{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED: PB-3 at exact head 1979a37fc737ec4b9cc7534afefce466c05c9ce1, tree 949152f0f3b22d9b097edea59537a7e2ade833ff, over published main 12cb8fa7.\n\nVerified: The nine artifacts equal the nine changed paths. Commit d3df3f1c..1979a37f adds only the implementation note. The gate log SHA-256 8b3a3150… matches the file, and gate END fa42172c passed every stage at d3df3f1c. check-commit-messages flags 0 of 5 commits. diff --check is clean, and the head merges cleanly onto origin/main. The ReadSessions fix meets condition 1 of 709615ff: an `aborted` flag and a listener Set, with no workerd I/O object. The named red and green for hosted.scope.test.ts are retained.\n\nTwo findings block approval.\n\n1. With renewal off, the client re-enters each time its own row expires, and that fills the scope faster than renewal would. In `scheduleNext` and `act` (live-presence.ts, about lines 476-551), `fields` stays set after the first enter. When the timed `expire` rule moves the own row to its final state, the summary no longer lists it, so `selectOwnRow` returns null. Then `!own` schedules a new act of kind `enter`. An open view with no user change therefore expires and re-enters about every 45 s. Before LL-1, each cycle retains about 4,263 bytes for the final card (from df7515e2), plus the cost of the enter itself. At 50 members, that is about 80 cycles per member-hour, roughly 17 MB per hour, so the scope is full in about 2 hours. Renewal at 15 s fills it in about 5 hours. The note says renewal stays off \"so long-running live scopes do not fill their retained budget\", and this path contradicts that statement. Members also flicker out and back in every 45 s. No test covers it: the native witness keeps Alice alive by update (live-presence-client.test.ts line 388), and the scripted test advances only 30 s. Fix: after the client's own row expires while the view is open, do not re-enter automatically. Emit a state such as `expired`, and re-enter only on the next `set()` or an explicit call. Add a scripted test that advances past the lease with unchanged fields and asserts that no second enter is signed. If the planner prefers re-entry, state the retained-bytes cost in the note and get that ruling.\n\n2. Request a294276d asks the lifecycle to leave \"on teardown and page hide\". The module leaves on `close()` only. It has no `pagehide` or `visibilitychange` handling, and the note does not mention page hide. Either add an opt-in page-hide hook that sends the leave without waiting, or state in the note that the caller wires `pagehide` to `close()`, and say why.\n\nNot blocking: the note publishes the absolute path `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/`. One note on main already does, so this follows precedent. A relative label such as `artroom-evidence/` would be better.\n\nArchitecture: Sound apart from finding 1. One module provides the watch and the lifecycle. Reads come from notices, with no pre-act reads. B4 stays on projected offers, and the note explains why.\nSecurity: Sound. Signing stays with the caller's `sign`. A refusal is never answered with a guessed revision. The session cache holds no cross-context I/O object.\nSimplification: No objection beyond the findings.\nWake rate: No alarm is added on the room side. The client has one debounce timer and one backoff timer per open view. Measured traffic: 240 acts and 240 summary reads per tab-hour at 1 tab, and 6,000 aggregate summary reads per hour at 5 tabs (n-squared fan-out). Finding 1 adds about 80 enters per member-hour while renewal is off.\n\nA documents-only change for finding 2 needs no gate rerun. A source change for finding 1 needs its test red first and a full gate at the new head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b0b8e611b739ec89db652701cb85ff0de738ee64","binding":"assigned","head":"1979a37fc737ec4b9cc7534afefce466c05c9ce1","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5c3e00d7f5b3db71cf00c24babaed903aa06a18d\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9418515c1fa6e91fb86a6964136da4933bde9960\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4a1760ee742382755a70e4059b377929d13af9e2","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}